IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei4-part-vii-benefit-repayment`

-- Tests of ei4-part-vii-benefit-repayment.l4 (Act ss 144 to 152). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the section,
-- before the module was run; none is copied from the module's output. Every dollar figure is invented for the test; none is a published
-- maximum yearly insurable earnings. Worked example used throughout: maximum yearly insurable earnings 60,000, so 1.25 times is 75,000.

§ `Fixtures: benefits paid in the taxation year`

-- Regular benefits under Part I: counted by s 145(1)(a).
`a regular Part I payment of 20000` MEANS `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year` WITH
    `the amount paid` IS 20000
    `the Part under which the benefit is payable` IS `Part I`
    `the reason for which the benefit is paid` IS `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`

-- Regular benefits under Part VIII (fishing): "benefits" read without reference to Part VII, so counted too.
`a regular Part VIII payment of 3000` MEANS `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year` WITH
    `the amount paid` IS 3000
    `the Part under which the benefit is payable` IS `Part VIII`
    `the reason for which the benefit is paid` IS `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`

-- Regular benefits under Part VIII (fishing), a smaller payment.
`a regular Part VIII payment of 1000` MEANS `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year` WITH
    `the amount paid` IS 1000
    `the Part under which the benefit is payable` IS `Part VIII`
    `the reason for which the benefit is paid` IS `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`

-- Maternity benefits under Part I: special benefits, left out by s 145(1)(a).
`a maternity Part I payment of 8000` MEANS `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year` WITH
    `the amount paid` IS 8000
    `the Part under which the benefit is payable` IS `Part I`
    `the reason for which the benefit is paid` IS `pregnancy`

-- A Part VII.1 payment: left out by s 145(1)(a) even when its reason is a regular one (the text lists the two exclusions separately).
`a Part VII.1 payment of 5000` MEANS `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year` WITH
    `the amount paid` IS 5000
    `the Part under which the benefit is payable` IS `Part VII.1`
    `the reason for which the benefit is paid` IS `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`

-- A Part VIII.4 payment: not "benefits" as s 2(1) defines them (Part I, VII.1 or VIII only), so not counted.
`a Part VIII.4 payment of 1000` MEANS `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year` WITH
    `the amount paid` IS 1000
    `the Part under which the benefit is payable` IS `Part VIII.4`
    `the reason for which the benefit is paid` IS `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`

`the payments of 20000 regular benefits` MEANS LIST `a regular Part I payment of 20000`
`the payments of 30000 regular benefits` MEANS LIST `a regular Part I payment of 20000`, `a regular Part VIII payment of 3000`, `a regular Part VIII payment of 3000`, `a regular Part VIII payment of 3000`, `a regular Part VIII payment of 1000`

`a mixed year of payments` MEANS LIST `a regular Part I payment of 20000`, `a regular Part VIII payment of 3000`, `a maternity Part I payment of 8000`, `a Part VII.1 payment of 5000`, `a Part VIII.4 payment of 1000`

§ `s 144 -- definitions`

-- 144 "benefits": unemployment benefits payable under Part I, VII.1 or VIII (s 2(1)); not Part VIII.4.
#ASSERT `s 144 benefits` `Part I`
#ASSERT `s 144 benefits` `Part VIII`
#ASSERT NOT `s 144 benefits` `Part VIII.4`
-- 144 "income": ITA income 80000, plus deductions 3000 added back, less 1000 (s 79 gain) and 500 (s 56): 81500.
#ASSERT `s 144 income of a person for a period` 80000 3000 1000 500 EQUALS 81500
-- 144 "income": nothing to adjust leaves the Income Tax Act figure.
#ASSERT `s 144 income of a person for a period` 80000 0 0 0 EQUALS 80000
-- 144 "Minister": the Minister of National Revenue in Part VII.
#ASSERT `s 144 the Minister for this Part` EQUALS `the Minister of National Revenue`

§ `s 145(1)(a) -- the benefits counted`

-- 145(1)(a): Part I regular (20000) and Part VIII regular (3000) count; maternity, Part VII.1 and Part VIII.4 do not.
#ASSERT `s 145(1)(a) the total benefits, other than special benefits and benefits under Part VII.1, paid to the claimant in the taxation year` `a mixed year of payments` EQUALS 23000
-- 145(1)(a): no payments, no total.
#ASSERT `s 145(1)(a) the total benefits, other than special benefits and benefits under Part VII.1, paid to the claimant in the taxation year` EMPTY EQUALS 0
-- 145(1)(a): a list of only excluded payments totals nothing.
#ASSERT `s 145(1)(a) the total benefits, other than special benefits and benefits under Part VII.1, paid to the claimant in the taxation year` (LIST `a maternity Part I payment of 8000`, `a Part VII.1 payment of 5000`) EQUALS 0

§ `s 145(1)(b) and (1) -- income over 1.25 times the maximum`

-- 145(1)(b): income 100000, maximum 60000: 1.25 x 60000 = 75000; the excess is 25000.
#ASSERT `s 145(1)(b) the amount by which the claimant's income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings` 100000 60000 EQUALS 25000
-- 145(1): income 100000 exceeds 75000.
#ASSERT `s 145(1) the claimant's income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings` 100000 60000
-- 145(1): income of exactly 75000 does not "exceed" it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(1) the claimant's income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings` 75000 60000
-- 145(1): one dollar over does.
#ASSERT `s 145(1) the claimant's income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings` 75001 60000
-- 145(1) worked example: benefits 20000, excess 25000: 30% of the lesser (20000) is 6000.
#ASSERT `s 145(1) the repayment before the exception in subsection (2)` `the payments of 20000 regular benefits` 100000 60000 EQUALS 6000
-- 145(1): benefits 30000 exceed the excess 25000: 30% of the lesser (25000) is 7500.
#ASSERT `s 145(1) the repayment before the exception in subsection (2)` `the payments of 30000 regular benefits` 100000 60000 EQUALS 7500
-- 145(1): the lesser is the excess when the excess is small: income 76000, excess 1000, benefits 20000: 30% of 1000 is 300.
#ASSERT `s 145(1) the repayment before the exception in subsection (2)` `the payments of 20000 regular benefits` 76000 60000 EQUALS 300
-- 145(1): income exactly at the threshold: no repayment is required.
#ASSERT `s 145(1) the repayment before the exception in subsection (2)` `the payments of 20000 regular benefits` 75000 60000 EQUALS 0
-- 145(1): the mixed year: only 23000 counts, and the excess (25000) is the larger; so 30% of 23000 is 6900.
#ASSERT `s 145(1) the repayment before the exception in subsection (2)` `a mixed year of payments` 100000 60000 EQUALS 6900
-- Finding 5: nothing in Part VII rounds. An excess of one cent gives 30% of one cent, not zero and not a whole dollar.
#ASSERT `s 145(1) the repayment before the exception in subsection (2)` `the payments of 20000 regular benefits` 75000.01 60000 EQUALS 0.003

§ `s 145(2) and (3) -- the exception, and weeks before 30 June 1996`

-- 145(3): the date is June 30, 1996; a week beginning on 29 June 1996 (or earlier) is left out, one beginning on 30 June is counted.
#ASSERT `s 145(3) June 30, 1996` EQUALS YearMonthDay 1996 6 30
#ASSERT `s 145(3) the week is excluded because it begins before June 30, 1996` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 29)
#ASSERT `s 145(3) the week is excluded because it begins before June 30, 1996` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 23)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(3) the week is excluded because it begins before June 30, 1996` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(3) the week is excluded because it begins before June 30, 1996` (YearMonthDay 1996 7 7)
-- Finding 7: 30 June 1996 is a Sunday, the first day of a week (s 2(1) "week"), so the week beginning on that day is the first one counted.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 30) EQUALS YearMonthDay 1996 6 30
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` (YearMonthDay 1996 6 29) EQUALS YearMonthDay 1996 6 23
-- 145(3): twelve weeks paid in the ten years, five of them beginning before 30 June 1996: seven count.
#ASSERT `s 145(3) the weeks of regular benefits taken into account when applying subsection (2)` 12 5 EQUALS 7
-- 145(3): if every week paid began before 30 June 1996, none counts.
#ASSERT `s 145(3) the weeks of regular benefits taken into account when applying subsection (2)` 5 5 EQUALS 0
-- 145(2): "less than one week": none paid, the exception applies; one week paid, it does not.
#ASSERT `s 145(2) subsection (1) does not apply because the claimant was paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before the taxation year` 0
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(2) subsection (1) does not apply because the claimant was paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before the taxation year` 1
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(2) subsection (1) does not apply because the claimant was paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before the taxation year` 3
-- 145: the benefit repayment. With three weeks counted the worked example gives 6000; with none the exception takes it away.
#ASSERT `s 145 the benefit repayment` `the payments of 20000 regular benefits` 100000 60000 3 EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT `s 145 the benefit repayment` `the payments of 20000 regular benefits` 100000 60000 0 EQUALS 0
-- 145: exactly one week counted is not "less than one week".
#ASSERT `s 145 the benefit repayment` `the payments of 20000 regular benefits` 100000 60000 1 EQUALS 6000
-- 145: income at the threshold: nothing, whatever the weeks.
#ASSERT `s 145 the benefit repayment` `the payments of 20000 regular benefits` 75000 60000 10 EQUALS 0

§ `s 145(4) -- time for repayment`

-- 145(4)(a): death on 1 November 2025 is "after October" in 2025; death on 31 October is not.
#ASSERT `s 145(4)(a) the claimant dies after October in the year and before May in the next year` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 11 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(4)(a) the claimant dies after October in the year and before May in the next year` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 10 31))
-- 145(4)(a): death on 30 April 2026 is "before May" in the next year; death on 1 May is not.
#ASSERT `s 145(4)(a) the claimant dies after October in the year and before May in the next year` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30))
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(4)(a) the claimant dies after October in the year and before May in the next year` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1))
-- 145(4)(a): a claimant who has not died is not in this case.
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(4)(a) the claimant dies after October in the year and before May in the next year` 2025 NOTHING
-- 145(4)(b): April 30 in the next year.
#ASSERT `s 145(4)(b) April 30 in the next year` 2025 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30
-- 145(4)(a): six months after the day of death: 30 November 2025 gives 30 May 2026; 31 December 2025 gives 30 June 2026 (no 31 June).
#ASSERT `s 145(4)(a) the last day within six months after the day of death` (YearMonthDay 2025 11 30) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 30
#ASSERT `s 145(4)(a) the last day within six months after the day of death` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 30
-- 145(4): a claimant who is alive: April 30 of the next year.
#ASSERT `s 145(4) the last day on which the repayment must be made` 2025 NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30
-- 145(4): died 15 December 2025: within six months, 15 June 2026.
#ASSERT `s 145(4) the last day on which the repayment must be made` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 15
-- 145(4)(b): died 31 October 2025, outside (a): any other case, April 30 2026.
#ASSERT `s 145(4) the last day on which the repayment must be made` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 10 31)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30
-- 145(4)(b): died on 1 November 2025, inside (a): six months after, 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `s 145(4) the last day on which the repayment must be made` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 11 1)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1
-- 145(4)(a): died on 30 April 2026, still inside: 30 October 2026.
#ASSERT `s 145(4) the last day on which the repayment must be made` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 10 30
-- 145(4)(b): died on 1 May 2026, outside (a): the April 30 rule.
#ASSERT `s 145(4) the last day on which the repayment must be made` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30

§ `s 145(5) to (8) -- limitation, and repealed subsections`

-- 145(5): a repayment under section 145 does not affect the weeks of regular benefits counted under (2).
#ASSERT `s 145(5) the repayment affects the determination under subsection (2) of regular benefits paid` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 145(5): a repayment of some other kind: the subsection says nothing. NOT COVERED: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 145(5) the repayment affects the determination under subsection (2) of regular benefits paid` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#EVAL `s 145(6) to (8) repealed, and therefore not encoded`

§ `s 146 -- returns`

-- 146: a claimant is required to make a repayment when there is one to make.
#ASSERT `s 146 the claimant is required to make a benefit repayment for the taxation year` 6000
#ASSERT NOT `s 146 the claimant is required to make a benefit repayment for the taxation year` 0
-- 146(a): dies 15 December 2025, in the window "after October 31 ... before May 1".
#ASSERT `s 146(a) the claimant dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15))
#ASSERT NOT `s 146(a) the claimant dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 10 31))
#ASSERT NOT `s 146(a) the claimant dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year` 2025 NOTHING
-- Finding 6: s 145(4)(a) and s 146(a) say the same window in different words; the two rules agree on the edges.
#ASSERT `s 145(4)(a) the claimant dies after October in the year and before May in the next year` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 11 1)) EQUALS `s 146(a) the claimant dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 11 1))
#ASSERT `s 145(4)(a) the claimant dies after October in the year and before May in the next year` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)) EQUALS `s 146(a) the claimant dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1))
-- 146(a): the legal representative has six months after the day of death.
#ASSERT `s 146(a) the last day for the legal representative to file the return` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 15
-- 146(b): the claimant's filing-due date for the year.
#ASSERT `s 146(b) the last day for the claimant to file the return` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30
-- 146: the last day. A living claimant: the filing-due date.
#ASSERT `s 146 the last day on which the return must be filed` 2025 NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30
-- 146(a): a claimant who died 15 December 2025: the legal representative, six months after death.
#ASSERT `s 146 the last day on which the return must be filed` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15)) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 15
-- 146(b): a claimant who died 31 October 2025 is "any other claimant": the filing-due date.
#ASSERT `s 146 the last day on which the return must be filed` 2025 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 10 31)) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30
-- 146(c): the Minister's written notice names a day: that day counts (fork F-ei4-15).
#ASSERT `s 146 the last day on which the return must be filed` 2025 NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 9 1
-- 146: who files. An ordinary claimant files for themselves.
#ASSERT `s 146 who must file the return` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 146(b) the claimant files the return`
-- 146(a): the legal representative of a claimant who died in the window.
#ASSERT `s 146 who must file the return` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 146(a) the legal representative of the deceased claimant files the return`
-- 146(b): the guardian, curator, tutor, committee or other legal representative of a claimant who is unable to file.
#ASSERT `s 146 who must file the return` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 146(b) the guardian, curator, tutor, committee or other legal representative of a claimant who is unable to file files the return`
-- 146(c): the person the Minister requires by written notice, after the claimant or representative has not filed.
#ASSERT `s 146 who must file the return` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 146(c) the person required by notice in writing from the Minister files the return`
#ASSERT `s 146 who must file the return` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 146(c) the person required by notice in writing from the Minister files the return`

§ `ss 147 to 152`

-- 147: whoever must file under s 146 must estimate the benefit repayment in the return.
#ASSERT `s 147 the return must contain the person's estimate of the benefit repayment payable` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 147 the return must contain the person's estimate of the benefit repayment payable` FALSE
-- 148: the Minister (of National Revenue) administers and enforces Part VII.
#ASSERT `s 148 the office that administers and enforces this Part` EQUALS `the Minister of National Revenue`
-- 149: twelve entries of the Income Tax Act provisions that apply, as the section lists them.
#ASSERT count (`s 149 the provisions of the Income Tax Act that apply for the purposes of Part VII`) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT elem "Division J of Part I" (`s 149 the provisions of the Income Tax Act that apply for the purposes of Part VII`)
-- 149(a) to (d): the readings.
#ASSERT `s 149(a) to (d) what the word of the Income Tax Act is read as` "Act" EQUALS JUST "Part VII of the Employment Insurance Act"
#ASSERT `s 149(a) to (d) what the word of the Income Tax Act is read as` "person" EQUALS JUST "claimant"
#ASSERT `s 149(a) to (d) what the word of the Income Tax Act is read as` "taxpayer" EQUALS JUST "claimant"
#ASSERT `s 149(a) to (d) what the word of the Income Tax Act is read as` "tax" EQUALS JUST "benefit repayment"
#ASSERT `s 149(a) to (d) what the word of the Income Tax Act is read as` "taxes" EQUALS JUST "benefit repayment"
#ASSERT `s 149(a) to (d) what the word of the Income Tax Act is read as` "under this Part" EQUALS JUST "under Part VII of the Employment Insurance Act"
-- 149: a word the section does not list has no reading here. NOT COVERED: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 149(a) to (d) what the word of the Income Tax Act is read as` "interest" EQUALS NOTHING
-- 150: a benefit repayment (or an amount payable under the Income Tax Act's provisions as applied) is a debt due to Her Majesty.
#ASSERT `s 150 the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 150 the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 150 the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` FALSE FALSE
-- 150: recoverable in the Federal Court, in any other court of competent jurisdiction, or as the Income Tax Act provides.
#ASSERT `s 150 the ways in which the debt due to Her Majesty is recoverable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (LIST `s 150 in the Federal Court`, `s 150 in any other court of competent jurisdiction`, `s 150 in any other manner provided by the Income Tax Act`)
-- 150: an amount outside the section: it says nothing about recovery. NOT COVERED: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 150 the ways in which the debt due to Her Majesty is recoverable` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 151(1): tax information needed for Part VII or for section 43, given to the Commission.
#ASSERT `s 151(1) the Minister may communicate, or allow to be communicated, the information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 151(1) the Minister may communicate, or allow to be communicated, the information` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 151(1) the Minister may communicate, or allow to be communicated, the information` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 151(1) the Minister may communicate, or allow to be communicated, the information` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 151(1) the Minister may communicate, or allow to be communicated, the information` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 151(2): the person authorized by the Commission, in relation to information obtained under (1), is an official under the Income Tax Act.
#ASSERT `s 151(2) the person is an official or authorized person within the meaning of subsection 241(10) of the Income Tax Act and is subject to subsections 239(2.2) and 241(1) and (2) of that Act` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 151(2) the person is an official or authorized person within the meaning of subsection 241(10) of the Income Tax Act and is subject to subsections 239(2.2) and 241(1) and (2) of that Act` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 151(2) the person is an official or authorized person within the meaning of subsection 241(10) of the Income Tax Act and is subject to subsections 239(2.2) and 241(1) and (2) of that Act` FALSE TRUE
